<title>USA: U.S. Feb personal income rose 0.9 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Feb personal income rose 0.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Commerce Department personal income and spending estimates, in seasonally adjusted annual rates.</p>
<p>    Percent Changes:    Feb    Jan--(Prev)   Dec--(Prev)   Nov</p>
<p> Income (Current Dlrs)  0.9    0.4    0.3    0.7    0.7    0.6</p>
<p>Disposable Income:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.8    0.7    0.6    0.7    0.7    0.6</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.6    0.6    0.5    0.5    0.5    0.4</p>
<p>Consumption:</p>
<p> -- Current Dlrs	  0.3    1.0    0.7    0.4    0.2    0.4</p>
<p> -- Chain '92 Dlrs	0.1    0.9    0.6    0.2   Unch    0.2</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Feb    Jan--(Prev)   Dec--(Prev)   Nov</p>
<p> Income		   6,713  6,655  6,653  6,631  6,633  6,586</p>
<p> Disposable Income    5,825  5,777  5,774  5,737  5,737  5,699</p>
<p> Personal Outlays     5,503  5,484  5,464  5,428  5,426  5,408</p>
<p> Pers.Consumption     5,334  5,316  5,296  5,261  5,259  5,241</p>
<p> -Durable Goods	   652    652    643    637    633    637</p>
<p> -Non-Durable Goods   1,596  1,590  1,572  1,571  1,567  1,566</p>
<p> -Services		3,086  3,074  3,081  3,053  3,059  3,038</p>
<p> Personal Savings	 322    293    309    308    311    290</p>
<p> Pct Savings Rate	 5.5    5.1    5.4    5.4    5.4    5.1</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:   Feb    Jan--(Prev)   Dec--(Prev)   Nov</p>
<p> Wages and Salaries   3,801  3,751  3,751  3,753  3,755  3,714</p>
<p> -Manufacturing	   692    689    690    692    693    683</p>
<p> -Service Industries  1,341  1,316  1,318  1,320  1,322  1,299</p>
<p> -Government		658    654    653    647    648    647</p>
<p> Proprietors' Income    537    535    534    533    533    532</p>
<p> -Farm			 45     47     47     48     48     50</p>
<p> -Non-Farm		  492    488    487    485    485    482</p>
<p>Wall Street economists expected February personal income to rise 0.8 percent and spending to be up 0.4 percent.  </p>
<p>The department said that the 0.9 percent increase in personal income was the largest since an identical increase in June 1996. It said the personal savings rate, which rose 5.5 percent, was the largest level since 5.6 percent in September 1996.</p>
